# Sanctum Lurker keeps only the planeswalkers its controller controls ("Planeswalkers you control"). Bot2's Liliana of the
# Veil, cast on turn 2 and down to 1 loyalty after a −2 at Bot2 itself (it has no creature to sacrifice), takes 3 damage
# from Bot1's Lightning Bolt on turn 3: damage to a planeswalker removes that many loyalty counters (CR 120.3c), and at 0
# loyalty it is put into Bot2's graveyard (CR 704.5i) though Bot1 controls a Lurker. Bot1's own Jace token, also at 0, is
# the control that stays. Nor does the Lurker give Bot2's Liliana its "[+2]" ("Planeswalkers you control have"): it is
# refused there, while Jace, Bot1's, is offered it (sanctum-lurker-keeps-a-jace-at-zero-loyalty-that-then-uses-its-plus-two).

